diff --git a/port/linux/embed/README.md b/port/linux/embed/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..61961fa
--- /dev/null
+++ b/port/linux/embed/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,176 @@
+# YouGame native X11 embedding
+
+`yougame_embed_x11.h` + `yougame_embed_x11.c` reparent a native game's existing
+X11 window into the desktop app's player box. C99; Xlib and libXext only. The
+first intended host is Melee Unlocked's SDL2 Linux build. This implements the
+Orca child-window approach, with keyboard focus deliberately given to the game.
+
+The child has a black background, no border or decorations, and an empty XShape
+INPUT region: pointer events hit the app underneath. Keys still reach the game
+when explicitly focused. A child is outside the window manager's top-level
+management, so the helper withdraws the old top-level and reparents it; it sets
+override-redirect to false rather than relying on it. The existing title is
+retained as metadata and has no separate title bar while embedded.
+
+## Wire contract
+
+The app supplies `YOUGAME_EMBED=1`, `YOUGAME_EMBED_PARENT=<decimal X11 Window>`,
+and access to that parent's X display through `DISPLAY`. X11 or XWayland is
+required for both processes. A native Wayland SDL window cannot be attached.
+Missing/invalid environment, an unreachable parent or unavailable Shape 1.1
+returns NULL; the host shows its ordinary standalone window instead.
+
+The host's existing stdin reader forwards complete lines, optionally including
+the `embed ` prefix. The helper never reads stdin or consumes X events itself.
+
+| Line | Effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| `embed rect x y w h` | Move/resize in parent-relative X11 pixels; valid rect initially maps the child. |
+| `embed show` / `embed hide` | Show/hide intent; rect updates preserve an explicit hide. |
+| `embed focus` | Give the visible child X keyboard focus; retain the request if hidden. |
+| `embed blur` | Return keyboard focus to the parent when viewable. |
+| `embed quit` | Return `YG_EMBED_QUIT`; host exits cleanly. |
+| `embed volume 0..1` | Validate and return OK; host applies the actual audio gain. |
+
+On Linux the origin is the Electron X11 window's inside top-left, **not** screen
+coordinates or the web page's top-left. The page already converts CSS pixels
+using devicePixelRatio, and `native.ts` calls `frameRectLine` to add the Linux
+menu-bar offset to y. Apply neither a second scale nor another title/menu offset.
+Sources: `desktop/src/native.ts:1083-1088,1418-1420`,
+`desktop/src/orca-policy.ts:1280-1283`, `desktop/src/main.ts:675-692`,
+`web/src/lib/desktop.ts:115`.
+
+Both dimensions must be at least 32 to display. Smaller dimensions, including
+zero/negative, hide without resizing; `show` cannot override that. A subsequent
+valid rect restores the requested visibility. Coordinates are signed 16-bit;
+dimensions are capped at 16384. Overflow, malformed numbers, extra tokens,
+unknown commands and lines longer than 159 bytes return `YG_EMBED_IGNORED`
+without changing state. Volume accepts decimal notation only. Zero-size layouts
+never reach the renderer. Sizes reported while hidden retain the last real size.
+
+## SDL2 host integration
+
+1. Build this C file with the host; link `-lX11 -lXext`. In embedded launches,
+   select SDL's `x11` video backend **before SDL_Init** (e.g. SDL_SetHint with
+   SDL_HINT_VIDEODRIVER where supported, or the launch environment). Use the same
+   DISPLAY as the app. Do not switch a running SDL video backend.
+2. Create the window with `SDL_WINDOW_HIDDEN | SDL_WINDOW_OPENGL` immediately
+   before attaching. Avoid fullscreen, mouse capture, relative mouse mode and
+   keyboard grabs in embedded mode. A 24-bit opaque visual is preferred; for an
+   ARGB visual the helper sets an opaque black background, but the renderer must
+   also write alpha 1 (or disable framebuffer alpha) to keep rendered frames opaque.
+3. Immediately after `SDL_CreateWindow`, get `SDL_SysWMinfo` and attach, before
+   showing the window/creating the GL context. On NULL, call SDL_ShowWindow and
+   keep the normal standalone path. With an attached helper, let it own window
+   mapping, placement and focus; do not call SDL_ShowWindow/HideWindow/SetWindowSize
+   or SDL_SetWindowFullscreen on that path.
+
+```c
+#include <SDL.h>
+#include <SDL_syswm.h>
+#include "yougame_embed_x11.h"
+
+/* window was just created hidden; all this runs on the video/Display thread. */
+SDL_SysWMinfo wm;
+SDL_VERSION(&wm.version);
+yg_embed_x11 *embed = NULL;
+if (SDL_GetWindowWMInfo(window, &wm) && wm.subsystem == SDL_SYSWM_X11)
+    embed = yg_embed_x11_attach(wm.info.x11.display, wm.info.x11.window);
+if (embed) SDL_EventState(SDL_SYSWMEVENT, SDL_ENABLE);
+else SDL_ShowWindow(window);
+/* Now create/make current the host's GL context as usual. */
+```
+
+4. Queue complete stdin lines from your reader onto the video thread; call
+   `yg_embed_x11_command(embed, line)` there. Do not call Xlib from the reader
+   thread. Bound your line accumulator and discard a whole overlong line, not
+   separate truncated commands. Handle volume in the host's existing audio
+   command path, using a strict finite 0..1 parser; the helper has no audio API.
+   Treat stdin EOF as quit for an embedded run. Continue routing other stdio
+   bridge commands through the host's existing handler.
+5. In the SDL_PollEvent loop, forward **every** SDL_SYSWMEVENT for X11 immediately,
+   including the foreign parent's events. Do not filter by the SDL game window
+   id or retain the SDL_SysWMmsg pointer after processing the event. Leave SDL in
+   charge of reading its Display; do not add a competing XNextEvent loop.
+
+```c
+int running = 1;
+SDL_Event ev;
+while (running && SDL_PollEvent(&ev)) {
+    if (embed && ev.type == SDL_SYSWMEVENT && ev.syswm.msg &&
+        ev.syswm.msg->subsystem == SDL_SYSWM_X11 &&
+        yg_embed_x11_event(embed, &ev.syswm.msg->msg.x11.event) == YG_EMBED_QUIT)
+        running = 0;
+    if (ev.type == SDL_QUIT) running = 0;
+    if (embed && ev.type == SDL_KEYDOWN && !ev.key.repeat &&
+        ev.key.keysym.sym == SDLK_ESCAPE) {
+        fputs("yg {\"key\":\"escape\"}\n", stdout);
+        fflush(stdout);
+    }
+    /* Existing host input handling follows; stop rendering if running == 0. */
+}
+/* Also set running=0 when a queued stdin command returns YG_EMBED_QUIT. */
+```
+
+SDL2 forwards SysWM events before looking up its own window, so parent events
+can use this route ([SDL2 X11 event source](https://github.com/libsdl-org/SDL/blob/SDL2/src/video/x11/SDL_x11events.c#L814-L862)).
+Confirm this with the SDL version linked into the Linux host.
+
+6. After draining stdin commands and SDL events, query the size. With the GL
+   context current, change the viewport/render targets only when dimensions
+   change. A move/restack ConfigureNotify must not recreate a swapchain.
+
+```c
+int w, h; /* viewport_w / viewport_h are host-owned cached dimensions. */
+if (running && yg_embed_x11_size(embed, &w, &h) &&
+    (w != viewport_w || h != viewport_h)) {
+    glViewport(0, 0, w, h); /* Or resize the host's Vulkan surface/render targets. */
+    viewport_w = w;
+    viewport_h = h;
+}
+```
+
+7. On QUIT (command, parent/child destruction, or detected vanished window), stop
+   input/render submission immediately, save and shut down through the host's
+   normal exit path. Call detach before destroying the SDL window/Display, and
+   discard the helper pointer. Parent destruction has already destroyed the X11
+   child; do not render another frame or try to show it as a standalone window.
+   Verify SDL/GL teardown on that path on the target build. For a deliberate live
+   detach, detach restores root parenting, original geometry, border, event
+   masks, input shape, Motif hints and original mapped state; call SDL_ShowWindow
+   afterward if the original window was hidden. The background remains black.
+
+All APIs are confined to the Display-owning thread. Serialize **all process-wide
+Xlib activity**, including SDL/GL calls on other threads, during helper calls:
+XSetErrorHandler is process-global. Traps cover helper-issued requests and sync
+before restoring the previous handler; they cannot guard arbitrary later SDL
+requests or a disconnected X server. Do not call from an SDL event filter while
+SDL is itself replacing the X error handler. One helper per game/parent per
+Display; detach restores the event selections saved at attach.
+
+## Demo and build
+
+On Linux with X11 development headers/libraries already installed:
+
+```sh
+make
+./demo
+```
+
+The Xlib-only demo creates its own fake app parent and child on DISPLAY. It prints
+PASS/FAIL for attachment, shape, rect/show/focus/blur/hide, validation, too-small
+handling, parent destruction/QUIT, safe detach and stale-parent fallback. It
+exits nonzero on failure. Run on an agent test display; it changes keyboard focus
+to its own windows briefly. No SDL or desktop app is needed for this smoke test.
+
+For XQuartz headers under `/opt/X11/include`, compile-only check:
+
+```sh
+cc -std=c99 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -I/opt/X11/include -c yougame_embed_x11.c demo.c
+```
+
+On this Mac the equivalent headers/libraries are in `/opt/homebrew`:
+
+```sh
+make CPPFLAGS=-I/opt/homebrew/include LDFLAGS=-L/opt/homebrew/lib
+```
diff --git a/port/linux/embed/yougame_embed_x11.c b/port/linux/embed/yougame_embed_x11.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0cb921c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/port/linux/embed/yougame_embed_x11.c
@@ -0,0 +1,353 @@
+#include "yougame_embed_x11.h"
+#include "../../runtime/hle/yougame_embed_view.h"
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <X11/Xatom.h>
+#include <X11/Xutil.h>
+#include <X11/extensions/shape.h>
+#include <ctype.h>
+#include <errno.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+struct yg_embed_x11 {
+    Display *dpy;
+    Window game, parent, root;
+    XWindowAttributes old;
+    long parent_mask;
+    int old_x, old_y, w, h, x, y;
+    int valid, shown, mapped, focus, viewable, dead;
+    Atom motif, motif_type;
+    int motif_format;
+    unsigned long motif_n;
+    unsigned char *motif_data;
+    XRectangle *shape;
+    int shape_n, shape_order;
+    XRectangle *bounding;
+    int bounding_n, bounding_order;
+    yg_embed_view_state layout;
+};
+
+/* Scoped, synchronous trap: unrelated requests retain the host's handler.
+ * The process must not issue concurrent Xlib requests or replace the handler. */
+static struct {
+    Display *dpy;
+    unsigned long first;
+    int failed, gone;
+    XErrorHandler previous;
+} trap;
+
+static int on_error(Display *dpy, XErrorEvent *ev)
+{
+    if (dpy != trap.dpy || ev->serial < trap.first)
+        return trap.previous ? trap.previous(dpy, ev) : 0;
+    trap.failed = 1;
+    if (ev->error_code == BadWindow || ev->error_code == BadDrawable)
+        trap.gone = 1;
+    return 0;
+}
+
+static void begin(Display *dpy)
+{
+    trap.dpy = dpy;
+    trap.first = NextRequest(dpy);
+    trap.failed = trap.gone = 0;
+    trap.previous = XSetErrorHandler(on_error);
+}
+
+static int end(Display *dpy)
+{
+    XSync(dpy, False);
+    XSetErrorHandler(trap.previous);
+    return trap.failed;
+}
+
+static int refresh(yg_embed_x11 *e)
+{
+    XWindowAttributes a;
+    if (!XGetWindowAttributes(e->dpy, e->parent, &a)) {
+        e->dead = 1;
+        return 0;
+    }
+    e->viewable = a.map_state == IsViewable;
+    return 1;
+}
+
+static void focus(yg_embed_x11 *e, int force)
+{
+    Window current;
+    int revert;
+    if (!e->focus || !e->mapped || !e->viewable) return;
+    XGetInputFocus(e->dpy, &current, &revert);
+    if (force || current == e->parent || current == e->game)
+        XSetInputFocus(e->dpy, e->game, RevertToParent, CurrentTime);
+}
+
+static void visibility(yg_embed_x11 *e)
+{
+    int map = e->shown && e->valid;
+    if (map && !e->mapped) XMapRaised(e->dpy, e->game);
+    if (!map && e->mapped) XUnmapWindow(e->dpy, e->game);
+    e->mapped = map;
+}
+
+yg_embed_x11 *yg_embed_x11_attach(Display *dpy, Window game)
+{
+    const char *enabled = getenv("YOUGAME_EMBED");
+    const char *id = getenv("YOUGAME_EMBED_PARENT");
+    char *tail;
+    unsigned long parent, left;
+    Window child;
+    XWindowAttributes app, own;
+    int major, minor, event, error, ok;
+    yg_embed_x11 *e;
+    if (!dpy || !game || !enabled || strcmp(enabled, "1") || !id || !*id)
+        return NULL;
+    for (tail = (char *)id; *tail; ++tail)
+        if (!isdigit((unsigned char)*tail)) return NULL;
+    errno = 0;
+    parent = strtoul(id, &tail, 10);
+    if (errno || *tail || !parent || parent > 0xffffffffUL || parent == game)
+        return NULL;
+    e = calloc(1, sizeof(*e));
+    if (!e) return NULL;
+    e->dpy = dpy; e->game = game; e->parent = parent;
+    begin(dpy);
+    ok = XGetWindowAttributes(dpy, parent, &app) &&
+         XGetWindowAttributes(dpy, game, &own) && app.root == own.root &&
+         app.class == InputOutput && own.class == InputOutput && parent != app.root &&
+         XShapeQueryExtension(dpy, &event, &error) &&
+         XShapeQueryVersion(dpy, &major, &minor) && (major > 1 || (major == 1 && minor >= 1));
+    if (end(dpy) || !ok) { free(e); return NULL; }
+    e->old = own; e->root = own.root; e->parent_mask = app.your_event_mask;
+    e->w = own.width; e->h = own.height; e->shown = 1;
+    e->layout = yg_embed_view_init(own.width, own.height, 32);
+    e->viewable = app.map_state == IsViewable;
+    begin(dpy);
+    e->motif = XInternAtom(dpy, "_MOTIF_WM_HINTS", False);
+    ok = XTranslateCoordinates(dpy, game, e->root, 0, 0, &e->old_x, &e->old_y, &child);
+    ok = ok && XGetWindowProperty(dpy, game, e->motif, 0, 1024, False, AnyPropertyType,
+         &e->motif_type, &e->motif_format, &e->motif_n, &left, &e->motif_data) == Success;
+    e->shape = XShapeGetRectangles(dpy, game, ShapeInput, &e->shape_n, &e->shape_order);
+    e->bounding = XShapeGetRectangles(dpy, game, ShapeBounding, &e->bounding_n, &e->bounding_order);
+    if (end(dpy) || !ok || left || (!e->shape && e->shape_n != 0) ||
+        (!e->bounding && e->bounding_n != 0)) {
+        XFree(e->bounding); XFree(e->shape); XFree(e->motif_data); free(e); return NULL;
+    }
+    begin(dpy);
+    XWithdrawWindow(dpy, game, XScreenNumberOfScreen(own.screen));
+    XSelectInput(dpy, parent, app.your_event_mask | StructureNotifyMask | FocusChangeMask);
+    XSelectInput(dpy, game, own.your_event_mask | StructureNotifyMask | FocusChangeMask);
+    {
+        unsigned long hints[5] = { 2, 0, 0, 0, 0 }; /* MWM_HINTS_DECORATIONS: none */
+        XChangeProperty(dpy, game, e->motif, e->motif, 32, PropModeReplace,
+                        (unsigned char *)hints, 5);
+    }
+    /* A non-root child is outside WM management; no override-redirect needed. */
+    {
+        XSetWindowAttributes a;
+        a.override_redirect = False;
+        XChangeWindowAttributes(dpy, game, CWOverrideRedirect, &a);
+    }
+    XSetWindowBorderWidth(dpy, game, 0);
+    XSetWindowBackground(dpy, game, own.depth == 32 ? 0xff000000UL : BlackPixelOfScreen(own.screen));
+    XClearWindow(dpy, game);
+    XShapeCombineRectangles(dpy, game, ShapeInput, 0, 0, NULL, 0, ShapeSet, Unsorted);
+    XReparentWindow(dpy, game, parent, 0, 0);
+    if (end(dpy)) { yg_embed_x11_detach(e); return NULL; }
+    return e;
+}
+
+static int number(const char *s, int *out)
+{
+    char *tail;
+    long n;
+    errno = 0;
+    n = strtol(s, &tail, 10);
+    if (errno || tail == s || *tail || n < -32768 || n > 32767) return 0;
+    *out = (int)n;
+    return 1;
+}
+
+int yg_embed_x11_command(yg_embed_x11 *e, const char *line)
+{
+    char buf[160], *args[6], *p;
+    size_t len = 0;
+    int n = 0, x = 0, y = 0, w = 0, h = 0, force = 0;
+    if (!e || !line) return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    if (e->dead) return YG_EMBED_QUIT;
+    while (len < sizeof(buf) && line[len]) ++len;
+    if (len == sizeof(buf)) return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    memcpy(buf, line, len + 1);
+    p = buf;
+    while (*p) {
+        while (isspace((unsigned char)*p)) ++p;
+        if (!*p) break;
+        if (n == 6) return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+        args[n++] = p;
+        while (*p && !isspace((unsigned char)*p)) ++p;
+        if (*p) *p++ = '\0';
+    }
+    if (n && !strcmp(args[0], "embed")) {
+        --n;
+        memmove(args, args + 1, (size_t)n * sizeof(*args));
+    }
+    if (!n) return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    if (n == 1 && !strcmp(args[0], "quit")) return YG_EMBED_QUIT;
+    if (n == 2 && !strcmp(args[0], "volume")) {
+        int dots = 0, digits = 0, whole = 0, fraction = 0;
+        for (p = args[1]; *p; ++p) {
+            if (*p == '.' && !dots) ++dots;
+            else if (*p >= '0' && *p <= '9') {
+                ++digits;
+                if (dots) fraction |= *p != '0';
+                else if (whole < 2) whole = whole * 10 + (*p - '0');
+            }
+            else return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+        }
+        return digits && whole <= 1 && !(whole == 1 && fraction)
+               ? YG_EMBED_OK : YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    }
+    if (!strcmp(args[0], "rect") || !strcmp(args[0], "view")) {
+        if (n != 5 || !number(args[1], &x) || !number(args[2], &y) ||
+            !number(args[3], &w) || !number(args[4], &h) || w > 16384 || h > 16384 ||
+            (!strcmp(args[0], "view") && (x < 0 || y < 0 || w < 0 || h < 0)))
+            return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    } else if (n != 1 || (strcmp(args[0], "show") && strcmp(args[0], "hide") &&
+               strcmp(args[0], "focus") && strcmp(args[0], "blur")))
+        return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    begin(e->dpy);
+    if (refresh(e)) {
+        if (!strcmp(args[0], "rect") || !strcmp(args[0], "view")) {
+            const int is_view = !strcmp(args[0], "view");
+            const yg_embed_box box = {x, y, w, h};
+            yg_embed_view_result result;
+            /* Preserve the legacy actual-size comparison without a view. Once
+             * a view owns layout, late ConfigureNotify events must not turn a
+             * rect-only clip into another resize request. */
+            if (!e->layout.has_view) {
+                e->layout.window.w = e->w; e->layout.window.h = e->h;
+            }
+            result = yg_embed_view_update(&e->layout, box, is_view);
+            e->valid = result.valid;
+            if (is_view) fprintf(stderr, "embed: view %d %d %d %d\n", x, y, w, h);
+            if (result.warn_clamp) fprintf(stderr, "embed: rect outside view; clamped to view\n");
+            if (e->layout.has_view) {
+                XRectangle clip;
+                clip.x = (short)result.clip.x; clip.y = (short)result.clip.y;
+                clip.width = (unsigned short)result.clip.w;
+                clip.height = (unsigned short)result.clip.h;
+                XShapeCombineRectangles(e->dpy, e->game, ShapeBounding, 0, 0,
+                                        &clip, 1, ShapeSet, Unsorted);
+                if (!result.resize)
+                    fprintf(stderr, "embed: clip %d %d %d %d (no resize)\n",
+                            result.clip.x, result.clip.y, result.clip.w, result.clip.h);
+            }
+            if (result.geometry) {
+                const yg_embed_box window = result.window;
+                if (result.resize) XResizeWindow(e->dpy, e->game, window.w, window.h);
+                if (window.x != e->x || window.y != e->y)
+                    XMoveWindow(e->dpy, e->game, window.x, window.y);
+                e->x = window.x; e->y = window.y; e->w = window.w; e->h = window.h;
+                XRaiseWindow(e->dpy, e->game);
+            }
+        } else if (!strcmp(args[0], "show")) {
+            e->shown = 1; yg_embed_view_show(&e->layout, 1);
+        } else if (!strcmp(args[0], "hide")) {
+            e->shown = 0; yg_embed_view_show(&e->layout, 0);
+        }
+        else if (!strcmp(args[0], "focus")) { e->focus = 1; force = 1; }
+        else if (!strcmp(args[0], "blur")) {
+            e->focus = 0;
+            if (e->viewable) XSetInputFocus(e->dpy, e->parent, RevertToParent, CurrentTime);
+        }
+        visibility(e);
+        focus(e, force);
+    }
+    end(e->dpy);
+    if (trap.gone) e->dead = 1;
+    return e->dead ? YG_EMBED_QUIT : YG_EMBED_OK;
+}
+
+int yg_embed_x11_event(yg_embed_x11 *e, const XEvent *ev)
+{
+    if (!e || !ev || ev->xany.display != e->dpy) return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    if (e->dead) return YG_EMBED_QUIT;
+    /* Synthetic events cannot establish destruction, mapping or geometry. */
+    if (ev->xany.send_event) return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    if (ev->type == DestroyNotify &&
+        (ev->xdestroywindow.window == e->parent || ev->xdestroywindow.window == e->game)) {
+        e->dead = 1;
+        return YG_EMBED_QUIT;
+    }
+    if (ev->type == ConfigureNotify && ev->xconfigure.window == e->game) {
+        if (ev->xconfigure.width != e->w || ev->xconfigure.height != e->h) {
+            e->w = ev->xconfigure.width; e->h = ev->xconfigure.height;
+        }
+        return YG_EMBED_OK;
+    }
+    if (ev->xany.window != e->parent || (ev->type != MapNotify &&
+        ev->type != UnmapNotify && ev->type != FocusIn && ev->type != FocusOut))
+        return YG_EMBED_IGNORED;
+    begin(e->dpy);
+    if (refresh(e)) {
+        if (e->mapped) XRaiseWindow(e->dpy, e->game);
+        /* Never pull keyboard focus back from another application. */
+        if (ev->type != FocusOut) focus(e, 0);
+    }
+    end(e->dpy);
+    if (trap.gone) e->dead = 1;
+    return e->dead ? YG_EMBED_QUIT : YG_EMBED_OK;
+}
+
+void yg_embed_x11_detach(yg_embed_x11 *e)
+{
+    XWindowAttributes a;
+    if (!e) return;
+    begin(e->dpy);
+    /* Query even after death: safe if a failed attach left the game alive. */
+    if (XGetWindowAttributes(e->dpy, e->game, &a)) {
+        XSetWindowAttributes restore;
+        XUnmapWindow(e->dpy, e->game);
+        XReparentWindow(e->dpy, e->game, e->root,
+                        e->old_x - e->old.border_width, e->old_y - e->old.border_width);
+        restore.override_redirect = e->old.override_redirect;
+        XChangeWindowAttributes(e->dpy, e->game, CWOverrideRedirect, &restore);
+        XSetWindowBorderWidth(e->dpy, e->game, e->old.border_width);
+        XResizeWindow(e->dpy, e->game, e->old.width, e->old.height);
+        XSelectInput(e->dpy, e->game, e->old.your_event_mask);
+        if (e->shape_n == 1 && e->shape[0].x == 0 && e->shape[0].y == 0 &&
+            e->shape[0].width == e->old.width && e->shape[0].height == e->old.height)
+            XShapeCombineMask(e->dpy, e->game, ShapeInput, 0, 0, None, ShapeSet);
+        else XShapeCombineRectangles(e->dpy, e->game, ShapeInput, 0, 0, e->shape,
+                                     e->shape_n, ShapeSet, e->shape_order);
+        if (e->layout.has_view) {
+            if (e->bounding_n == 1 && e->bounding[0].x == 0 && e->bounding[0].y == 0 &&
+                e->bounding[0].width == e->old.width && e->bounding[0].height == e->old.height)
+                XShapeCombineMask(e->dpy, e->game, ShapeBounding, 0, 0, None, ShapeSet);
+            else XShapeCombineRectangles(e->dpy, e->game, ShapeBounding, 0, 0, e->bounding,
+                                         e->bounding_n, ShapeSet, e->bounding_order);
+        }
+        if (e->motif_type != None)
+            XChangeProperty(e->dpy, e->game, e->motif, e->motif_type, e->motif_format,
+                            PropModeReplace, e->motif_data, (int)e->motif_n);
+        else XDeleteProperty(e->dpy, e->game, e->motif);
+        if (e->old.map_state != IsUnmapped) XMapWindow(e->dpy, e->game);
+    }
+    if (XGetWindowAttributes(e->dpy, e->parent, &a))
+        XSelectInput(e->dpy, e->parent, e->parent_mask);
+    end(e->dpy);
+    XFree(e->bounding); XFree(e->shape); XFree(e->motif_data); free(e);
+}
+
+int yg_embed_x11_size(const yg_embed_x11 *e, int *w, int *h)
+{
+    if (!e || e->dead) return 0;
+    if (w) *w = e->w;
+    if (h) *h = e->h;
+    return 1;
+}
+
+int yg_embed_x11_visible(const yg_embed_x11 *e)
+{
+    return e && !e->dead && e->shown && e->valid;
+}
diff --git a/port/linux/embed/yougame_embed_x11.h b/port/linux/embed/yougame_embed_x11.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c9817db
--- /dev/null
+++ b/port/linux/embed/yougame_embed_x11.h
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+#ifndef YOUGAME_EMBED_X11_H
+#define YOUGAME_EMBED_X11_H
+
+#include <X11/Xlib.h>
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+extern "C" {
+#endif
+
+typedef struct yg_embed_x11 yg_embed_x11;
+enum { YG_EMBED_OK = 0, YG_EMBED_IGNORED = 1, YG_EMBED_QUIT = 2 };
+
+/* All calls on the Display-owning thread; serialize process-wide Xlib activity
+ * during calls (XSetErrorHandler is global). No event reading or SDL dependency.
+ * NULL: disabled/invalid env, unreachable parent, unsupported ShapeInput, failure.
+ * Attach a hidden, ordinary SDL X11 window before showing it or rendering. */
+yg_embed_x11 *yg_embed_x11_attach(Display *dpy, Window game);
+/* One bounded, NUL-terminated line, optionally prefixed "embed ". Volume is a
+ * validated no-op: the host applies audio gain. Too-small rects hide the child. */
+int yg_embed_x11_command(yg_embed_x11 *e, const char *line);
+/* Feed every native X event, including events addressed to the parent. */
+int yg_embed_x11_event(yg_embed_x11 *e, const XEvent *ev);
+/* Restore a surviving window to a normal root child; NULL/destroy-safe. */
+void yg_embed_x11_detach(yg_embed_x11 *e);
+/* Returns 1 and the current pixel size, or 0 when absent/dead. Nullable outputs. */
+int yg_embed_x11_size(const yg_embed_x11 *e, int *w, int *h);
+/* Accepted rect/view intersection and explicit show/hide intent. */
+int yg_embed_x11_visible(const yg_embed_x11 *e);
+
+#ifdef __cplusplus
+}
+#endif
+#endif
