+# M7-0956: 0.9.56 source integration; staging build blocked
+
+The working tree integrates local fork `9b43b9e` into Mac `0792675`. No Git
+index/ref operations were performed. `sourceport/extern/melee` was not modified.
+The actual common ancestor is `c422e167`; merging from there preserves the Mac
+foundation that predates `b9b3c3b` and was absent from the Linux fork. A merge
+from `b9b3c3b` alone would remove the ELF loader and platform compatibility code.
+
+Three overlapping edits needed resolution: SDL F1 routing combines the embedded
+menu rule with the fork's stdio menu rule; window teardown cancels an overlay
+press and retains Mac fullscreen/embed cleanup; Unix `select()` uses `fd + 1`
+on both Darwin and Linux. The renderer retains GL 4.1, asynchronous translation,
+split prewarm, fullscreen and player-box swap hooks. On Mac a successful real
+frame swap emits ready without depending on a foreign NSPanel's stale SDL
+visibility flag. Caps and Shift+Tab down/up/cancel use the fork's protocol.
+Escape handling remains embedded relay, fullscreen exit, then the window menu.
+
+The loader scans executable ELF segments before mapping/binding/initializers,
+requires zero Linux canary accesses, and never patches instructions or allocates
+a fake canary. There is no legacy stack-protector path. Strong imports use an
+explicit supported-function table; symbols and relocation counts come from ELF
+metadata. Missing relocation tables are allowed. Unsupported imports/types fail.
+
+The full host's v20 API includes `h_card_boot_confirm`. It calls the shared
+YouGame policy, and logs the first accepted decisions 5 and 7. The retained game
+patch skips the create question and successful-created message, using the normal
+save creation/write path. `check_full.py memory-card` starts without a card folder,
+keeps its stdio pipe open without any network service, requires both decisions,
+a GALE01 save, and scene progress; it records the scene sequence. This has NOT
+been executed on the new Mac host.
+
+The Linux WebSocket shim is linked into the Mac full build. Darwin uses the
+system CommonCrypto/Security implementations rather than adding OpenSSL, and
+links the existing system iconv for the fork's text conversion. The stdio broker
+path is retained. All protocol checks are offline.
+
+`build_full.py` defaults to the supplied `mu-0956-linux-game-nosp/melee_game.so`;
+`MELEE_GAME_LIBRARY` overrides it. Packaging uses that file's sibling snapexcl
+and complete Sys directory. The builder remains direct Apple clang, two workers,
+15% memory gate, x86-64, deployment target 15.0. Packaging is unsigned and checks
+for symlinks. A build version/hash manifest prevents packaging or testing an old
+host as 0.9.56. Legacy M1/M2 scripts and historical results in README are not M7
+entry points.
+
+## Evidence collected without executing a game
+
+Evidence directory: `build-mac-full/m7-0956/` (ignored build output).
+
+- `static-library.json`: new library 0 executable canary signatures; old library
+  5,928. New library has 53 dynamic symbols, 28 supported strong imports, 15 weak
+  imports, and 33,744 relocations (RELATIVE 33,701; absolute 11; GLOB_DAT 4;
+  JUMP_SLOT 28). This is a static audit, not a successful runtime load.
+- `python-checks.json`: digest comparison 5/5 and fork source regression 4/4.
+  Python syntax checks passed for six Mac scripts. Preprocessor nesting and
+  conflict-marker checks passed; `git -c core.whitespace=cr-at-eol diff --check`
+  passed.
+- `format-roundtrip.json`: Linux reference is 9,000 retraces, 7,200 unique match
+  frames, 76 non-host-frame fields. Decimal-to-named-hex conversion compared
+  7,200 frames with zero differing values. This is NOT Mac/Linux parity.
+  `compare_digest.py` handles both formats numerically, aligns by match_frame,
+  reports differing values and coverage, and rejects missing reference frames.
+- `seed-static.json`: retained scale-2 seed has 349 GLSL files and 748 valid
+  1,380-byte recipes. The shader generator/UID functions and cache family
+  `gx-gl410-v2-s2` are unchanged; the shared shader change only affects uniform
+  constants for shadow tint. Runtime seed hits are NOT proven. New per-unique-
+  stage hit/miss counters and a seeded hidden check make that proof measurable.
+
+## Refused step and pending validation
+
+The mandatory shared queue was attempted with priority 1 and label
+`melee-ports:m7-0956-build`, using `/usr/bin/true` as a queue access probe. The
+sandbox refused the queue ticket write under `$HOME/.cache/yg-heavy-slots`,
+queue cleanup writes, and sysctl. The build/test step was stopped. HOME was not
+changed to create a private queue and no direct compilation bypass was used.
+Terminating the owned queue process (`kill -TERM 80973`) was also refused. Its
+owner may need to clean up that waiting process. Details are in `refusal.txt`.
+
+No new staging bundle was produced. The pre-existing app was left untouched.
+Full units, embed checks, shader translation checks, first-boot card evidence,
+Mac/Linux parity and seed runtime verification remain pending.
+
+When the existing shared queue is available in an authorized environment, run
+from this worktree (each command must retain the shared queue):
+
+```sh
+queue=<agent-tools>
+export MELEE_GAME_LIBRARY=<data-drive>/build-out/melee-ports/mu-0956-linux-game-nosp/melee_game.so
+"$queue" run --prio 1 --label melee-ports:m7-0956-build -- python3 -B port/mac/build_full.py
+"$queue" run --prio 1 --label melee-ports:m7-0956-unit -- python3 -B port/mac/check_full.py unit
+"$queue" run --prio 1 --label melee-ports:m7-0956-embed -- python3 -B port/mac/check_embed.py
+"$queue" run --prio 1 --label melee-ports:m7-0956-translation -- python3 -B port/mac/check_full.py shaders
+"$queue" run --prio 1 --label melee-ports:m7-0956-card -- python3 -B port/mac/check_full.py memory-card
+"$queue" run --prio 1 --label melee-ports:m7-0956-parity -- python3 -B port/mac/check_full.py parity
+"$queue" run --prio 1 --label melee-ports:m7-0956-seed -- python3 -B port/mac/check_full.py graphics --seed --scale 2
+```
+
+Game checks use only the team disc, headless/hidden rendering, dummy audio,
+`--volume 0`, explicit throwaway HOME/XDG paths, and a 120-second timeout. All
+check logs fail on `slippi: logged in as`. The seeded rendered check requires
+nonzero shader cache hits and records translation misses as well as parity.
+The expected bundle is `build-mac-full/MeleeUnlocked.app`; its final size,
+minimum OS load commands and lack of symlinks still need verification.
+
+Proposed commit: `mac: integrate Melee Unlocked 0.9.56 with the no-stack-protector native game`
